Scenario A CSV profile set up for one book is not in the other
Description The headings of a CSV file from a bank are the same whichever
# account they describe, so a shared profile would save the second
# book its setting up. It is not shared. The same bank's layout
# being set up twice is the repetition this decision accepts: a
# book that cannot be opened, copied or carried to another machine
# on its own would be the permanent cost, and it is the larger one.
# The second book asks, and what it is told becomes its own profile.
Given books are as previous
Given saved profiles of Business are : SavedProfile
| Name         | Signature                                      |
| Example Bank | Posted Date,Description,Amount,Running Balance |
Given saved profiles of Personal are : SavedProfile
| Name | Signature |
Given the current book is : CurrentBook Vertical
| Name | Personal |
Given the file contains
"""
Posted Date,Description,Amount,Running Balance
01/15/2024,A SHOP,-45.00,1705.00
"""
When headers matched
Then profile recognised is : ProfileRecognition Vertical
| Name      | none  |
| Asked     | true  |
| MatchedBy | Alias |
# Business has a profile for this bank and Personal has none, so this file is
# read the way any unrecognised one is: the headings are matched against the
# alias table, and the user is asked to name the bank. Nothing reaches into
# the business book to find the answer already given there.

Attributes CurrentBook
| Attribute | Type | Default |
| Name      | Text |         |

