Scenario A bank number known to one book is unknown to the other
Description Two accounts at one bank, one business and one personal, have two
# different numbers and belong in two different books. Each book's
# account carries its own number, and a download is placed by the
# book that is open. Finding the number in the other book would post
# business money to a personal account.
Given books are as previous
Given the chart of accounts of Business is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path            | Type     | Placeholder | BankId    | AccountNumber |
| Assets:Checking | Checking | false       | 053000196 | 1111111111    |
Given the chart of accounts of Personal is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path            | Type     | Placeholder | BankId    | AccountNumber |
| Assets:Checking | Checking | false       | 053000196 | 2222222222    |
Given the current book is : CurrentBook Vertical
| Name | Personal |
When statement imported : OfxStatement Vertical
| BankId       | 053000196  |
| OfxAccountId | 1111111111 |
| OfxAcctType  | CHECKING   |
Then asked to choose an account for : UnknownAccount Vertical
| BankId       | 053000196  |
| OfxAccountId | 1111111111 |
| OfxAcctType  | CHECKING   |
| Suggestion   | none       |
# The number is on an account, but in the other book. No account in this one
# claims it, so the import asks, exactly as it would for a number no account
