Scenario Money moving between the two books is two transactions
Description A draw from the business is the case that makes people want one
# book. It is recorded as two transactions, one in each book, each
# balanced within its own. Equity is where it goes, because from the
# point of view of the business it is capital leaving and from the
# point of view of the household it is not income earned.
Details Nothing links the two records. Making the second is the work the two
# books cost, and it is a handful of transactions a year against the
# certainty that no business report includes household spending.
Given books are as previous
Given the chart of accounts of Business is : ChartOfAccounts
